# A list that only one way through a turn reads does not stand in front of the loop: what is undefined there and never read would send every turn into the other copy
# (a-list-that-only-one-way-through-a-turn-reads-is-asked-on-that-way-and-not-in-front-of-the-loop.ir). Where the value is PROVEN a list the front cannot fail by absence, only by the kind of its storage: it
# stands in front again: `(i & 3) === 3 ? 0 : r[i]` took 45 instructions a turn against 19.
# f1 = inOneArm
# RUN: walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = IsPristine {{*}} builtinClass=Array aspects=[Storage, Names]
# CHECK: isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# RUN(SHELL): run-in-shell globalThis.sink = print;
# SHELL: 375.25 378 NaN
